  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 182, 'In a clinic or hospital, raise a handoff problem with the charge nurse rather than arguing with the nurse at the bedside.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 183, 'If a parent emails a teacher angrily, wait until you''re calm, then reply with a short note offering a time to talk.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 184, 'In a family-run small business, keep work disagreements at work, and set a time to discuss them during business hours.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 185, 'On a remote team, turn on your camera for a tricky conversation so the other person can see your face.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 186, 'Stop yourself from replying in the middle of an argument in a team chat, and say you''ll follow up privately.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 187, 'Notice who on your team handles disagreements well, and borrow one of their phrases.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 188, 'Write the next step for an unresolved issue on a sticky note and put it where you will see it tomorrow morning.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 189, 'Before a meeting with a new client, think about how you will respond if they push back on something you propose.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 190, 'Respond to a coworker''s criticism of your work by asking for one example, then thanking them for it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 191, 'Spend a minute after work naming one disagreement that went better than you expected.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 192, 'Make a plan with your partner or roommate for how much time you will spend talking about work after you get home.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 193, 'Prepare one sentence for when you are interrupted in a meeting: "I''d like to finish that thought."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 194, 'Treat a disagreement with a coworker as a puzzle you are solving together, and say so out loud.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 195, 'If a disagreement involves money or contracts, put the key points in writing and run it past your manager.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 196, 'Hold back from correcting a coworker in front of customers or patients, and mention it privately later.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 197, 'On a long video meeting, turn off your self-view for a while so you can focus on what others are saying.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 198, 'Ask yourself if a disagreement is about values or just preferences, and adjust how hard you push.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 199, 'Agree to disagree on one small matter today and move on without needing the last word.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 200, 'Write a short list of ground rules for your team meetings, like "one person speaks at a time," and offer it at the next one.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 201, 'When an angry customer calls, write down their main complaint as they talk, so you can repeat it back accurately.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 202, 'Ask a coworker to repeat what they heard you say in a disagreement, to make sure your point came across.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 203, 'Name your own mood before a difficult meeting: tired, rushed or on edge, and plan around it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 204, 'Pause to drink a glass of water before you walk into a room where a conflict is waiting.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 205, 'Picture a disagreement settled and how you will feel afterward, and let that guide the words you choose.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 206, 'Check in with yourself on the drive or train home about one tense exchange, and decide if it needs a follow-up.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 207, 'At the end of your workday, close any open tabs or threads that you do not need to reply to.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 208, 'Practice a calm, short "no" in a mirror once today, so it is ready when someone asks for too much.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 209, 'Offer to take notes at a meeting where the team often disagrees, so the record is neutral.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 210, 'When your manager gives you a deadline you cannot meet, explain the tradeoff and ask which task should slip.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 211, 'Listen to a direct report''s complaint about a coworker without taking sides, and ask what they would like to happen.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 212, 'Remind yourself before your next shift that tense moments with customers are about the situation, not about you.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 213, 'Bring up a pet peeve about a shared fridge or microwave at a team meeting, framed as a request for everyone.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 214, 'Thank a teammate in front of others for their part in a project where credit might otherwise get muddled.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 215, 'If someone keeps taking your shifts or leaving you short, document the dates and talk to the scheduler.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 216, 'On a slow chat thread, check if your coworker is out or busy before assuming they are ignoring you.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 217, 'When a coworker uses an expression or gesture you find odd, ask what it means rather than taking offense.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 218, 'If a coworker''s behavior makes you feel threatened, leave the situation and tell your supervisor or security right away.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 219, 'Before talking to HR, ask yourself what outcome you are hoping for so you can say it clearly.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 220, 'Jot down what is at stake for the other person in a current work disagreement: time, reputation, workload or pride.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 221, 'Describe a coworker''s action in a single factual sentence, like "The bins were left in aisle four," before you decide how to raise it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 222, 'Wonder aloud with a coworker, "How do you think we got here?" when a project goes sideways.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 223, 'Paraphrase a client''s complaint back to them in a sentence before you offer any fix.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 224, 'Tell a teammate how a change affected your work, starting with "I," and leave out guesses about why they did it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 225, 'Pick up the phone for a disagreement that would take more than three emails to settle.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 226, 'Ask a coworker "Is now a good time?" before raising something tense, and offer another time if it isn''t.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 227, 'Script the first line of a talk with your manager about a disagreement: "I''d like your take on something I see differently."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 228, 'Sit back in your chair and loosen your shoulders when a meeting turns into a debate.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 229, 'Leave a heated message unread for fifteen minutes while you finish a small task, then open it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 230, 'Choose one coworker whose motives you doubt and look for one piece of evidence that they mean well.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 231, 'Start your reply in a disagreement with what you agree on: "You''re right that we''re short on time."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 232, 'Give a client a pair of options, a smaller scope by Friday or the full scope next week, and let them choose.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 233, 'Keep a running list of decisions from tense meetings in a shared document so nobody has to rely on memory.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 234, 'Ask a coworker you disagreed with, "How did that sit with you afterward?" and listen to the answer.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 235, 'Reach out with a short note after you were curt in a meeting: "I came across harder than I meant to."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 236, 'Ask your manager for fifteen minutes to explain a different view on a plan, and come with one suggestion.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 237, 'Tell a direct report one thing they''re doing well right before you raise the one thing that needs to change.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 238, 'Walk away from a customer who becomes threatening, keep yourself safe and get a manager or security.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 239, 'Write down the store or company policy you most often need to explain, so you can say it calmly and the same way each time.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 240, 'Suggest a shared calendar for meeting rooms or equipment if people keep double-booking them.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 241, 'When you present work that was a group effort, list everyone''s names on the first slide.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 242, 'Ask your manager to help prioritize when two people are asking you for conflicting things.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 243, 'Before sending a quick chat reply, ask yourself whether it could be misread as annoyance.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 244, 'Learn one cultural or regional holiday a coworker observes, and ask about it when the time comes.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 245, 'If a conflict involves discrimination, harassment or safety, bring it to HR rather than trying to resolve it yourself.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 246, 'Ask HR how the reporting process works before you file anything, so you know what to expect.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 247, 'Write your factual notes about a serious problem the same day it happens, while the details are fresh.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 248, 'Notice the urge to point out a coworker''s small mistake today, and let them find it on their own instead.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 249, 'Plan a walk or a call with a friend after work on a day you know will be tense, so you have somewhere to set it down.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 250, 'Scan your inbox for one message you have been avoiding because of a disagreement, and send a short, calm reply.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 251, 'Lower the stakes of a disagreement by saying, "This doesn''t have to be settled today."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 252, 'Ask a coworker who often disagrees with you to review your next proposal before it goes to the group.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 253, 'Bring a printed agenda to a meeting where emotions may run high, so you can steer back to it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 254, 'In a coffee shop or restaurant, ask the shift lead to settle a recurring dispute about tips or side work.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 255, 'In a dental office or clinic, raise scheduling conflicts at the morning huddle rather than in front of patients.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 256, 'On a school staff, bring up a shared-classroom disagreement at a planning period, not in front of students.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 257, 'On a trades crew, talk through a disagreement about how a job should be done at the truck, before you start.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 258, 'In a warehouse, raise a fairness issue about who gets the easier routes or zones with the supervisor, with dates in hand.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 259, 'Agree on a shared response time with your remote team so nobody reads silence as rudeness.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 260, 'Ask yourself what you would advise a friend to do in your work conflict, and consider doing that.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 261, 'Notice whether you are more irritable before lunch, and try to avoid hard conversations when you are hungry.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 262, 'After a disagreement with your manager is decided, tell them you will support the decision, even if you argued against it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 263, 'Help a new coworker learn how disagreements usually get handled on your team.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 264, 'When a client is upset, say "I understand why that would be frustrating," and then explain what happens next.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 265, 'If you lose your temper with a customer, apologize briefly and offer to get someone else to help them.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 266, 'Speak up kindly when a teammate is left out of the credit for a shared success.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 267, 'Ask for a short meeting to talk about workload if you notice your hours climbing for weeks.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 268, 'Read your chat messages from today and look for any that might have sounded sharper than you intended.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 269, 'Ask a coworker from another generation for advice on a work problem, and use one piece of it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 270, 'Practice how you would tell HR about a serious issue in three sentences, so it comes out clearly.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 271, 'Let a slow coworker finish their task at their pace today, and use the wait to take a breath.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 272, 'Stay off social media and group chats about a work frustration, and talk it over with a trusted friend instead.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 273, 'Ask yourself what part of a disagreement you would be willing to give up, and offer it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 274, 'Stand rather than sit for a tough phone call if it helps you keep your voice steady.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 275, 'Try a "both/and" answer in a disagreement today: "We can do both if we move the launch by a week."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 276, 'When someone tells you about a problem with your work, ask "What would you like me to do differently?"'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 277, 'Avoid discussing a disagreement with a coworker over text late at night, and save it for work hours.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 278, 'Begin a team meeting with one item everyone already agrees on to set a calmer tone.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 279, 'Reread an email from a coworker you dislike, and look for the actual request inside it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 280, 'Give yourself one minute of quiet after a hard customer interaction before you serve the next person.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 281, 'In a performance review where you disagree with a rating, ask what you could do differently in the coming months.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 282, 'When the holiday party planning gets tense, offer to take on one small task rather than debating every detail.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 283, 'During busy season, agree with your team that short tempers are understandable and try to start each shift fresh.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 284, 'As summer vacations pile up, ask your manager to post the coverage plan so nobody feels singled out.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 285, 'Look back over this challenge so far and pick the one habit that has made the biggest difference in your work conversations.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 286, 'Before your next annual planning meeting, list one past friction point and suggest a simple way to prevent it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 287, 'When a manager disagrees with you in public, stay calm in the moment and ask for a private talk later.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 288, 'Recognize when a coworker needs to vent rather than solve, and just listen for a few minutes.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 289, 'Ask a coworker to brainstorm with you on a whiteboard so the conversation focuses on the problem, not on each other.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 290, 'Ask yourself what the other person in a disagreement might be afraid of, and speak to that worry.'),
