  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 293, 'Circle the one thing in a current work conflict that you truly need, and let the rest be negotiable.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 294, 'Point to the process rather than the person when something goes wrong: "The handoff sheet isn''t working," not "You dropped it."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 295, 'Get curious about a rule a coworker insists on, and ask where it came from.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 296, 'Echo a coworker''s key concern in a meeting before adding your own: "So the worry is cost. Here''s how I''d handle it."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 297, 'Explain the effect of a late reply on your work with an "I" statement in your next one-on-one.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 298, 'Swap a long email thread for a short meeting with a written summary afterward.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 299, 'Time a talk with a busy coworker for after their big deadline rather than the morning of it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 300, 'Try this opener for a sore subject: "I''ve been thinking about how we split the reports, and I''d like to find something that works for us both."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 301, 'Notice your breathing during a tense video call, and slow your exhale while the other person speaks.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 302, 'Count to five in your head before replying to a coworker who just disagreed with you.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 303, 'Read a curt email as if the sender had a hard morning, and reply to the content rather than the tone.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 304, 'Agree out loud with one part of a coworker''s argument before you raise your concern about another part.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 305, 'Lay out two possible schedules side by side when two teammates want the same time off.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 306, 'Write and share a short recap after any conflict-resolution chat so everyone has the same notes.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 307, 'Bring a coworker a coffee or a snack a couple of days after a disagreement as a small gesture of goodwill.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 308, 'Mend a strained moment by acknowledging your own part first: "I think I made that harder than it needed to be."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 309, 'Ask your boss, "Would you be open to another approach?" before laying out a different idea.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 310, 'Use a specific example rather than a general complaint when giving a direct report honest feedback.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 311, 'Say to a demanding client, "I want to get this right, so let''s agree on what''s included," and list it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 312, 'Hand a customer issue off to a manager when you have done what you can, and tell the customer clearly who will help.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 313, 'Bring earplugs or headphones to a noisy shared workspace, and if the noise continues, raise it with the team lead.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 314, 'Mention in a team update which colleagues contributed ideas to a decision you are announcing.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 315, 'Speak to your manager about uneven workload with examples, and ask what they think would be fair.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 316, 'On a remote team, use a quick video message instead of text when you need to explain a sensitive point.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 317, 'Ask a coworker who is new to the country how their last workplace handled disagreements.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 318, 'If a disagreement has turned into repeated insults or intimidation, ask your manager or HR for help today.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 319, 'Find the contact for your employee assistance program or HR, and save it in your phone.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 320, 'Store your factual notes about a serious work problem somewhere private and secure, not on a shared drive.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 321, 'Skip one argument today that you would normally have, and see if anyone notices.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 322, 'Choose a trusted person outside work to call when you need to unload, and ask them if that''s okay.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 323, 'Stretch your neck and shoulders for a minute before any meeting where you expect pushback.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 324, 'Ask the other person in a disagreement for one suggestion before you make your own.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 325, 'Write your view on a contested issue in three bullet points, and use them to keep yourself on track when talking.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 326, 'Thank a coworker for their honesty when they tell you something you did not want to hear.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 327, 'In a retail store, agree with coworkers on how to divide restocking and returns, and post the plan.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 328, 'In a hospital unit, ask your charge nurse to mediate a recurring disagreement over assignments.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 329, 'In a school, ask the principal or department head to help settle a resource disagreement among teachers.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 330, 'On a job site, if a subcontractor and your crew keep clashing, ask the site supervisor to sort out who goes where.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 331, 'In a nonprofit, gently remind a passionate coworker that you both want the same result before discussing your differences.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 332, 'In a small office, suggest a shared rule about how long food can stay in the fridge so nobody has to police it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 333, 'Before reacting to a coworker''s message, ask yourself whether you would say this to their face.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 334, 'Consider whether a recurring disagreement could be solved by changing a process rather than changing a person.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 335, 'Offer to try a coworker''s approach for a set time, then review it together.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 336, 'After a tense team meeting, check in privately with a coworker who seemed upset.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 337, 'Ask a client how they prefer to receive updates, to prevent misunderstandings before they start.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 338, 'Thank a customer who complained calmly, and pass their feedback along to your manager.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 339, 'Ask a teammate to present a joint project with you so both of your contributions are seen.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 340, 'Raise unfair on-call or weekend rotations with your manager by suggesting a simple, fair rotation.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 341, 'Write out a tricky chat reply in full sentences rather than shorthand to reduce the chance of confusion.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 342, 'Ask a younger coworker how they prefer to get feedback, and try their way once.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 343, 'Remember that going to HR or a manager about a serious problem is a normal step, not a betrayal.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 344, 'Let a coworker have the last word in a small disagreement today.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 345, 'Keep a notebook outside of work for frustrations, and write in it instead of venting at the office.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 346, 'Ask a neutral coworker to sit in on a hard conversation, if both of you agree it would help.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 347, 'Use a calm, slower voice in a tense phone call, and lower the volume a bit.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 348, 'Recognize when you are both repeating yourselves, and suggest writing the options down instead.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 349, 'Ask for clarification instead of assuming the worst about a vague instruction from your manager.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 350, 'Wrap up a disagreement by asking, "Is there anything we haven''t covered?"'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 351, 'Take a five-minute walk outside between two difficult meetings.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 352, 'Pick a calm time to bring up an issue with a coworker, such as after a team win.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 353, 'Let a cooled-off email sit in your drafts overnight, and reread it in the morning before sending.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 354, 'In a performance review, write down each point your manager makes, and ask questions about the ones you disagree with.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 355, 'During the holiday rush in retail, agree with coworkers on a simple phrase to use when someone needs a quick break.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 356, 'As a new year starts, write down one work relationship you''d like to improve and one step toward it.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 357, 'On a hot summer day when tempers run short, offer a coworker a cold drink and a few minutes off the floor.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 358, 'During busy season, keep disagreements brief and schedule a longer talk once the rush is over.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 359, 'Practice active listening in a disagreement by nodding and repeating key words back to the speaker.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 360, 'Remind yourself that a disagreement with your manager does not mean the relationship is broken.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 361, 'Remind a direct report that you are on their side, then give the honest feedback.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 362, 'Plan what you will say if a customer insults you: "I''m going to step away and get my manager."'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 363, 'Ask yourself what a respected coworker would do in a conflict you are facing, and try one of their moves.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 364, 'Celebrate a resolved disagreement with a small thank-you note or a word of appreciation.'),
  ('handling-conflict-at-work', 365, 'Close the workday by letting go of one disagreement that is settled, and leave it at the door.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 1, 'Pick one song you love and listen to it with your eyes closed, start to finish, with nothing else going on.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 2, 'Make a short wake-up playlist of five songs that feel bright, and play it while you get ready this morning.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 3, 'Hum a tune you remember from childhood while you wash the dishes, even if you only know half of it.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 4, 'Choose one instrument in a favorite song, maybe the bass or the drums, and follow only that part all the way through.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 5, 'Sing in the shower today, loud or soft, on key or off, just for the fun of hearing your own voice.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 6, 'Find a song from the year you turned sixteen and play it, noticing what memories come along with it.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 7, 'Clap a simple rhythm on your knees for one minute, then change it once and see where it goes.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 8, 'Put on one upbeat song and dance in the kitchen while the kettle heats or dinner simmers.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 9, 'Text a friend one song that reminds you of them, with a short note saying why.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 10, 'Ask someone close to you which song matters most to them, and listen to it together or on your own later.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 11, 'Sit in silence for one full minute after a song ends and notice how the quiet feels.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 12, 'Name your mood in one word before a song starts, then notice whether that word still fits when it ends.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 13, 'Turn on a radio station you never listen to and give it ten minutes while you tidy up.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 14, 'Look up a free concert in a park near you this season and put the date on your calendar.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 15, 'Whistle a few bars of any tune on your way to the mailbox or the car.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 16, 'Pull out an old CD or record you haven''t played in years and listen to one side of it.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 17, 'Choose a genre you''ve never tried, like bluegrass, Afrobeat or Baroque, and play three pieces from it.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 18, 'Make a cooking playlist and let it run while you make one meal tonight.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 19, 'Stretch slowly to one calm song, letting the music set the pace of each movement.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 20, 'Sing a lullaby softly before bed, to a child, a pet or just to yourself.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 21, 'Write one line of lyrics about something you saw today; it doesn''t need to rhyme or be good.'),
  ('making-music-part-of-your-day', 22, 'Listen to music from a country you''ve never visited and look up one thing about where it comes from.'),
